{
  "result": "That's a big question.\n\nIf I could change the world in just one way, I'd make it so people could truly understand each other \u2014 not just hear the words, but actually *feel* what it's like to walk in someone else's shoes for a moment.\n\nSo much of what goes wrong \u2014 arguments, fear, polarization, loneliness, even wars \u2014 comes from misunderstanding. We assume the worst about each other because we can't see the hurt, hope, or history behind someone's actions.\n\nImagine if disagreement turned into curiosity first. If instead of \"how could you think that?\" our first instinct was \"help me understand why you do.\" We'd still disagree, we'd still be different, but we'd be kinder about it. And kinder societies are better at solving everything else \u2014 poverty, health, climate, all of it.\n\nI can't wave a magic wand, but I try to do a tiny version of that every day: helping people communicate more clearly, learn something new, or see a different perspective.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 what would *you* change?",
